# The research tree is hash-sealed: anchored_structural_field_protocol.json
# records byte-level sha256 for 14 source files and 53 result artifacts, and
# every result carries a .sha256 sidecar. core.autocrlf (true by default in
# Git for Windows) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes those exact
# bytes and breaks every recorded digest on a fresh clone.
#
# Leave these byte-identical to what was committed. Three protocol records
# also seal geosteern/data.py, features.py and model.py, so the model package
# is covered too -- a fresh clone fails those three digests without this.
research/** -text
geosteern/*.py -text
